SUMMARY:Speakeasy Casino Night
DTSTAMP:20260824T033959Z
DTSTART:20261002T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Houston Heights Association · Est. 1973\n        \n        Spea
	keasyCasino Nightin the Heights\n        \n          One night\, back in t
	he Prohibition era. Casino tables\, cocktails\, live\n          entertainm
	ent\, a silent auction and raffle — and the whole\n          neighborhood 
	in one room. Every dollar stays in the Heights.\n         \n\n        \n  
	        DateFriday\, October 2\, 2026\n          Time7:00 – 10:30 pm\n    
	      WhereThe Historic Houston Heights Fire Station107 W 12th Street\, Ho
	uston\, TX 77008\n          Admission$100 per guestIncludes gaming chips\,
	 food & drink\n        \n\n        \n          Get tickets — $100\n       
	   Become an underwriter\n        \n      \n\n      \n        \n      \n  
	  \n  \n\n  \n\n    \n    \n      Admission\n      \n        \n          O
	ne night only\n          Speakeasy Ticket\n          $100per guest\n      
	    \n            Entry for one\, 7:00 to 10:30 pm\n            Starting s
	tack of gaming chips for the tables\n            Heavy hors d’oeuvres and 
	cocktails\n            Live entertainment and dancing\n            Access 
	to the silent auction and raffle\n          \n        \n\n        \n      
	    How many are coming?\n          \n            −\n            \n       
	     +\n          \n          \n            1 ticket\n            $100.00\
	n          \n          \n            Add to cart →\n          \n        \n
	      \n    \n\n    \n    \n      The evening\n      What the night looks 
	like\n      \n        Doors at seven\, password at the door. Come dressed 
	for 1926 if you like —\n        flapper\, pinstripe\, or just your good ja
	cket.\n       \n      \n        \n          \n          Casino tables\n   
	       Blackjack\, roulette\, poker and craps\, run by dealers all evening
	. Chips come with your ticket. \n        \n        \n          \n         
	 Cocktails & bites\n          Period cocktails at the bar and heavy hors d
	’oeuvres circulating all night. \n        \n        \n          \n        
	  Silent auction & raffle\n          Neighborhood-donated packages\, exper
	iences and prizes — bid from your table. \n        \n        \n          \
	n          Live entertainment\n          Music\, dancing\, and a stage pro
	gram — plus a few surprises we’re not printing here. \n        \n      \n 
	   \n\n    \n    \n      Why it matters\n      \n        \n          A $40
	\,000 night for the neighborhood\n          \n            Casino Night is 
	a fundraiser first. What we raise on October 2 goes directly\n            
	into the programs neighbors actually see — the boulevard\, the parks\,\n  
	          the constable patrol\, the home tour\, and the small grants we m
	ake each spring.\n           \n          \n            More than 150 resid
	ents and guests are expected. The Houston Heights\n            Association
	 is a volunteer-led nonprofit\, and this is one of the few nights\n       
	     a year the whole neighborhood is in one room.\n           \n        \
	n        \n          $40\,000Fundraising goal\n          150+Neighbors exp
	ected\n          100%Stays in the Heights\n        \n      \n    \n\n    \
	n    \n      Sponsorship\n      Put your name on the night\n      \n      
	  Three underwriting levels\, each with tickets included and your name or 
